{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544415-spotlight-initiative","id":1544415,"title":"Spotlight Initiative","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-21T11:56:28-07:00","id":1544415,"title":"Spotlight Initiative","content":"Disappointed to still see this in the game. I don't know who's sacred cow this is, but you have to let it go. The spotlight system is terrible. It's slow and clunky, if one character goes first they all will and there are very few occasions where that won't be the case, you only need one character with a super high initiative, with the way it is you might as well just not have initiative at all, just let everyone pick the order of turns each round. A fixed initiative order with the ability to hold your turn until later in the round accomplishes the same thing they're trying to do with the spotlight system but better in every way. Seriously, the spotlight system needs to go away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T12:41:27-07:00","id":1544419,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately (or not if you're a fan) it seems to be built into SPU core so it's baked in. <br /> <br /> My only real problem with it is thatit involves rolling a bunch of individual initiative checks most of which will be useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T11:59:15-07:00","id":1544480,"title":"","content":"You can always use the dice rolls as a regular initiative pool if you'd like. I feel like Spotlight pretty much is meant to keep players active while its other's turns in case they get called to go next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T14:19:08-07:00","id":1544501,"title":"","content":"Yep, it keeps players involved and there are several adversary cases where you'll want the bad guy to act so you can respond in turn. It especially helps if your group like to plan a strategy. <br /> <br /> All that said, I'm sorry you don't like it, but it's the initiative system for all SPU games. You can dispense with it if it doesn't work for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T17:00:09-07:00","id":1544517,"title":"","content":"The other thing I'd say about Spotlight under SPU is that if I'm reading the system right it's extremely hard to deal more than one damage with an attack, which makes alpha-striking down a tough enemy (or group of tough-ish enemies) fairly unlikely.<br /> <br /> Ironically it seems easier to take out two one-health enemies with a single attack than to take out one two-health enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T19:58:35-07:00","id":1544527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544415-spotlight-initiative?p=1544517#post1544517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other thing I'd say about Spotlight under SPU is that if I'm reading the system right it's extremely hard to deal more than one damage with an attack, which makes alpha-striking down a tough enemy (or group of tough-ish enemies) fairly unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a good thing to me. I\u2019m most familiar with the WoD games and it had an extreme alpha-strike issue and so many character types could be killed with one or two hits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T03:45:29-07:00","id":1544541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544415-spotlight-initiative?p=1544527#post1544527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds like a good thing to me. I\u2019m most familiar with the WoD games and it had an extreme alpha-strike issue and so many character types could be killed with one or two hits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah I didn't mean that in a bad way. <br /> <br /> The big &quot;flaw&quot; of spotlight initiative is that it's easy for every PC to act before any NPC, but that's only a problem if it results in the NPC getting blown up in one round. Of it doesn't it's functionally no different from any other initiative system in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T05:21:47-07:00","id":1544544,"title":"","content":"I only see a problem if every adversary you face is operating solo and every player character is guaranteed to inflict an injury on their turn. Both of these situations are unlikely to be the default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T10:59:19-07:00","id":1544577,"title":"","content":"To clarify, I don't think Spotlight initiative is a problem. Although I will say that any initiative system which has a problem with solo adversaries (which honestly is most initiative systems) *is* going to have problems at some point because you can't just make every antagonist a group of interchangeable goons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T07:06:25-07:00","id":1545051,"title":"","content":"Now Adversaries are out:<br /> <br /> I think it's worth pointing out how huge Reaction Dread Powers are as part of this conversation. A major NPC or antagonist is very likely to have abilities which trigger *when PCs do stuff*.<br /> <br /> This has some problems for NPCs who can't force engagement (looking at you Haint) but this is massive for dealing with the alpha strike / action economy problem. Right now there are plenty of big monsters who can just plain eat you of you try to punch them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T13:48:49-07:00","id":1545068,"title":"","content":"Which I don't think really matters. They'd be able to do it regardless of when you act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27505-dragox27","name":"Dragox27","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27505_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T14:26:08-07:00","id":1545070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragox27</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544415-spotlight-initiative?p=1545068#post1545068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which I don't think really matters. They'd be able to do it regardless of when you act.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly why it matters.<br /> <br /> The big problem with Spotlight initiative is that there's a risk of one PC getting high Initiative, and then them just chaining their turns into an alpha strike that wipes your big scary antagonist before they can even do anything.<br /> <br /> But if they've got a bunch of Reaction abilities, then trying to blitz them down *first* doesn't actually help because you taking actions is what triggers most of their effects.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T16:05:15-07:00","id":1545077,"title":"","content":"You seem to agree that acting first is advantageous in general so then you should agree that the reactions don't matter. Because if they're doing their reactions whether or not you go first then it makes no difference. They'll happen in either case but as acting first is generally advantageous it remains advantageous. Those reactions aren't less punishing if you act second and are potentially more punishing. As these reaction come in the form of Complications then anything they could use their action on that would increase the chances of those occurring makes them worse for the PCs. Anything you can do on your action to mitigate those, such as activating something that would grant Enhancement, makes them less severe. Which I would say makes acting first advantageous. Reactions simply don't matter when it's a the same on both sides of this equation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27505-dragox27","name":"Dragox27","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27505_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T18:13:31-07:00","id":1545080,"title":"","content":"I'm confused about what you're saying here. <br /> <br /> Going first is probably still advantageous, but in a world where Reactions don't exist it is *dominating*, especially under Spotlight Initiative.<br /> <br /> With Reactions: The PCs win initiative, the NPC uses at least one reaction every time a PC does anything, there is a narratively satisfying feeling of back and forth and the PCs have to expend some resources or suffer some significant consequences. <br /> <br /> Without Reactions: The PCs win initiative, they alpha strike the NPC off the board. The NPC may as well not have existed.<br /> <br /> Reactions existing radically improves Spotlight initiative as a system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T18:18:14-07:00","id":1545081,"title":"","content":"I'm saying I think they're basically irrelevant to the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27505-dragox27","name":"Dragox27","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27505_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T18:25:25-07:00","id":1545082,"title":"","content":"Okay but... what do you think the point is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}